==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 4~16 seconds<sup>120f~480f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 10.67 seconds<sup>320f</sup>, delay 13.33~40 seconds<sup>400f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07~4 seconds<sup>2f~120f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
**20 [[Baa Baa]]s spawn, delay 0.07~2 seconds<sup>2f~60f</sup>.
**4 [[One Horn]]s spawn, delay 0.07~3.33 seconds<sup>2f~100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage isn't tough but can be for a beginner who doesn't have much firepower. It is recommended to use [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]] that can dish either crowd-control or dish out damage to the One Horns such as [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]], [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Viking Cat]] or [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Swordsman Cat]]. You can use [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] as well if you need more time to kill them.

The Teacher Bear is mainly a support for the One Horns and is not much of a threat. Killing a One Horn or the Baa Baas will also give you more money in order to kill the remaining enemies. Once you kill the One Horns, the Teacher Bear should be a piece of cake.

